{"id":"CVE-2021-23336","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"snyk","published":"2021-02-15T12:15:20.788Z","updated":"2026-10-14T11:34:52.993Z","title":"Web Cache Poisoning","description":"The package python/cpython from 0 and before 3.6.13, from 3.7.0 and before 3.7.10, from 3.8.0 and before 3.8.8, from 3.9.0 and before 3.9.2 are vulnerable to Web Cache Poisoning via urllib.parse.parse_qsl and urllib.parse.parse_qs by using a vector called parameter cloaking. When the attacker can separate query parameters using a semicolon (;), they can cause a difference in the interpretation of the request between the proxy (running with default configuration) and the server. This can result in malicious requests being cached as completely safe ones, as the proxy would usually not see the semicolon as a separator, and therefore would not include it in a cache key of an unkeyed parameter.","cwe":["Web Cache Poisoning","CWE-444 CWE-444 Inconsistent Interpretation of HTTP Requests ('HTTP Request/Response Smuggling')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.9,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H/E:P/RL:U/RC:C"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"python/cpython","versions":["affected 0 <unspecified (custom)","affected unspecified <3.6.13 (custom)","affected 3.7.0 <unspecified (custom)","affected unspecified <3.7.10 (custom)","affected 3.8.0 <unspecified (custom)","affected unspecified <3.8.8 (custom)","affected 3.9.0 <unspecified (custom)","affected unspecified <3.9.2 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-UPSTREAM-PYTHONCPYTHON-1074933"},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/24297"},{"url":"https://snyk.io/blog/cache-poisoning-in-popular-open-source-packages/"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2021/02/19/4","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[oss-security] 20210219 Django security releases: CVE-2021-23336: Web cache poisoning via ``django.utils.http.limited_parse_qsl()``"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2021/02/msg00030.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20210219 [SECURITY] [DLA 2569-1] python-django security update"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/HCQTCSP6SCVIYNIRUJC5X7YBVUHPLSC4/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-7547ad987f"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/NODWHDIFBQE5RU5PUWUVE47JOT5VCMJ2/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-f4fd9372c7"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/MP572OLHMS7MZO4KUPSCIMSZIA5IZZ62/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-3352c1c802"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/MNUN5SOMFL2BBKP6ZAICIIUPQKZDMGYO/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-7d3a9004e2"},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/rf9fa47ab66495c78bb4120b0754dd9531ca2ff0430f6685ac9b07772%40%3Cdev.mina.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[mina-dev] 20210225 [jira] [Created] (FTPSERVER-500) Security vulnerability in common/lib/log4j-1.2.17.jar"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/FONHJIOZOFD7CD35KZL6SVBUTMBPGZGA/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-907f3bacae"},{"url":"https://lists.fedorapro